What it does, in full:

- Installs into your own user profile, under
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\LatencyLab. It requires no administrator rights and
  writes nothing outside your profile.
- Creates the Desktop and Start Menu shortcuts you tick. No others.
- Registers an entry under HKEY_CURRENT_USER so the application appears in
  Apps and Features and can be removed from there.
- Keeps a copy of itself in the installation folder, which is what the
  Uninstall button runs.

It contacts no network, collects no data and sends nothing anywhere.

